        "check (the language finder raised this; it may not be a fault): 'Penisillien was die eerste antibiotikum uit 'n skimmel wat wyd gebruik': Grammatically 'wat' attaches to 'skimmel', so the sentence (and the identical heading) says the mould was widely used; the intent is that the antibiotic was. Reordering would touch a fact-checked claim, so a writer should decide.",
